+/*
+ * Nest J49 NAND env-WRITE recovery (2026-11-04). Dedicated, USB-DFU-booted
+ * recovery SPL that restores the FACTORY u-boot env into NAND env0 in the
+ * STOCK BCH4 ECC format so stock u-boot 2012.10 reads it (regdom/model/
+ * pairing vars -> WiFi + USB gadget come back). Unlike the env-ERASE hook,
+ * this runs AFTER omap3_mem_init(): it builds the full 0x20000 env image in
+ * DRAM (SRAM is only 64 KiB) at NEST_ENV_DRAM_BUF, erases env0+env1
+ * (blocks 26..31, abs 0x340000..0x400000), then programs the image into
+ * env0 (block 26, 64 pages) with per-page BCH4 syndromes at OOB 36..63.
+ * HARD-BOUNDED to the env blocks -> boot0 (0x400000, block 32)/root0 can
+ * never be touched. Worst case (wrong ECC) the env CRC simply fails and
+ * stock falls back to its built-in default env (today's degraded state),
+ * which is re-erasable; nothing outside the env region is written.
+ *
+ * NAND = Micron MT29F2G16ABBEAH4: x16, 2048-byte page, 64-byte OOB,
+ * 128 KiB block, 4 x 512-byte ECC sectors/page. GPMC CS0 is configured x16
+ * by gpmc_init()/set_gpmc_cs0() (M_NAND_GPMC_CONFIG1 = 0x1800, DEVICESIZE
+ * = 16-bit; CONFIG_SYS_NAND_BUSWIDTH_16BIT=y), so the data phase is 16-bit.
+ */
